631
00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:17.480
I couldn't have described it the way you

632
00:25:17.480 --> 00:25:17.780
did.

633
00:25:18.360 --> 00:25:19.560
You've said it so beautifully.

634
00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:22.500
I'm not educated enough to speak like that,

635
00:25:22.660 --> 00:25:25.140
she admitted timidly, her voice carrying a note

636
00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:27.560
of respect for what she called my pathetic

637
00:25:27.560 --> 00:25:30.200
eloquence and lofty style.

638
00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:35.080
But still, I'm glad, so very glad that

639
00:25:35.080 --> 00:25:36.520
you've been so open with me.

640
00:25:37.340 --> 00:25:39.240
Now I feel like I know you completely,

641
00:25:39.860 --> 00:25:40.860
every part of you.

642
00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:44.360
She paused, her dark eyes studying me closely,

643
00:25:44.940 --> 00:25:46.620
as if seeing me for the first time

644
00:25:46.620 --> 00:25:47.380
in a new light.

645
00:25:47.920 --> 00:25:50.680
And do you know what, she said, her

646
00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:52.980
tone shifting to one of quiet determination.

647
00:25:53.660 --> 00:25:55.600
I want to tell you my story too,

648
00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:58.000
everything with no secrets.

649
00:25:58.860 --> 00:26:01.040
After that, you must promise to give me

650
00:26:01.040 --> 00:26:01.460
advice.

651
00:26:01.920 --> 00:26:02.800
You're so clever.

652
00:26:03.460 --> 00:26:05.280
Will you promise to help me figure things

653
00:26:05.280 --> 00:26:05.600
out?

654
00:26:06.780 --> 00:26:10.460
Ah, Nastenka, I exclaimed, feeling a surge of

655
00:26:10.460 --> 00:26:11.580
emotion at her trust.

656
00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:14.060
I've never been much good at giving advice,

657
00:26:14.760 --> 00:26:16.880
sensible advice, least of all.

658
00:26:17.300 --> 00:26:20.600
But seeing us here now, like this, I

659
00:26:20.600 --> 00:26:22.960
feel as though, if we always stay this

660
00:26:22.960 --> 00:26:25.760
way, together, we'll both end up giving each

661
00:26:25.760 --> 00:26:28.540
other plenty of good advice, sensible or not.

662
00:26:29.140 --> 00:26:32.360
Tell me, my dear Nastenka, what kind of

663
00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:33.320
advice do you need?

664
00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:35.060
Speak openly.

665
00:26:35.960 --> 00:26:39.040
Right now I'm so happy, so light-hearted,

666
00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:41.800
so bold and clear-headed that I feel

667
00:26:41.800 --> 00:26:43.600
like I could find the right words for

668
00:26:43.600 --> 00:26:44.060
anything.

669
00:26:44.900 --> 00:26:49.580
No, no, Nastenka interrupted, laughing warmly, her earlier

670
00:26:49.580 --> 00:26:50.820
tears already forgotten.

671
00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:54.560
I don't just want sensible advice, I want

672
00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:57.580
advice that's warm and kind, advice that feels

673
00:26:57.580 --> 00:26:59.360
like it's coming from an older brother who

674
00:26:59.360 --> 00:27:01.060
has cared about me my whole life.

675
00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:03.360
That's the kind of advice I need?

676
00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:07.820
Agreed, Nastenka, agreed, I cried, delighted by her

677
00:27:07.820 --> 00:27:08.300
request.

678
00:27:08.800 --> 00:27:10.880
And let me tell you this, if I

679
00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:12.920
had known you all my life, if I

680
00:27:12.920 --> 00:27:15.560
had cared about you for twenty years, I

681
00:27:15.560 --> 00:27:17.560
still couldn't feel any fonder of you than

682
00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:18.260
I do now.

683
00:27:19.160 --> 00:27:22.080
Give me your hand, said Nastenka, her voice

684
00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:23.380
steady and filled with meaning.

685
00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:27.360
Here it is, I replied, placing my hand

686
00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:28.760
in hers without hesitation.

687
00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:31.360
She held it for a moment, her fingers

688
00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:33.560
gripping mine firmly, as if to seal some

689
00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:35.180
unspoken promise between us.

690
00:27:35.720 --> 00:27:38.280
Then she smiled, a smile so full of

691
00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:40.440
hope and trust that it seemed to light

692
00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:42.560
up the dim, quiet street around us.

693
00:27:43.580 --> 00:27:46.340
And now, she said, her voice soft but

694
00:27:46.340 --> 00:27:49.360
filled with anticipation, Let's begin my story.
